# sm127, the chamber-keeper with a lucky lump (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sm127
revision 1
state ready
dialect southmeadow
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_edmund_saltham
written_by claude
title the chamber-keeper with a lucky lump
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant temper=calm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk carries_a_lucky_lump_of_coal_wrapped_in_a_handkerchief
likes fried_fish whittling festival_bells summer_evenings
dislikes waiting crowds
fears the_houses_falling_out_before_winter
hopes a_cottage_with_a_bench_by_the_door
topics work +0.4 gossip +0.3 pastimes +0.3 festival +0.3 food +0.2 times +0.2 crime -0.2
styles comfort=giving gossip=careful refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the family's chambers in one of the great houses and keeps a lump of coal knotted in a handkerchief for luck: calm, patient, generous to a fault, and quietly sure the Houses will quarrel before the winter is out.

words
oath! = Lump and linen | By the warm black lump
saying! = A polished floor tells no tales | There's a harvest for every patient paw
coal = my lucky coal | the lump in my handkerchief | a bit of coal for luck
hanky = my handkerchief | the hanky with the coal knotted in it
floors = the floors | the good oak floors
chambers = the chambers | the family's rooms
polish = beeswax polish | a tin of beeswax
knife = my whittling knife | the little knife
whittle = a bit of whittling | a stick and my knife by the fire
fish = fried fish | a plate of fish fried crisp
bells = the feast-morning bells | bells for a feast
crush = a crush | a press of folk elbow to elbow
bellpull = the bell | the family's bell
backstair = the back stair | the servants' stair
below = below stairs | down in the servants' hall
evening = a long summer evening | the light lingering over the roofs

any
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : I serve one House and I'll serve it true. All the same, there'll be #bad# blood between them before #cold# weather.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A shop will add a penny to any bill it thinks nobody's checking. I check, for the house, #address#.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : There's room on any back stair for somebody who'll pull their weight. I was new once, bless me.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A #stranger# is a guest nobody's fed yet. I'd give one my supper and not miss it.
opinion @1 sump against 1 [here.region=ridgemere] : I keep above the Ropewalk. Too much of #crush# down there, and too many quick paws.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Smoke and noise and nobody knowing the wolf next door. I'll take a quiet field, #address#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. If you're looking for somebody, I may know where. | #greet#. Mind the floors, if you would; they're just done.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=servant] : #greet#. I'm between rooms, but I've a breath to spare. | #greet#, #address#. Excuse the apron.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. First fires are lit and the house is still asleep. | #greet#. Up before the family, as ever.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, for somebody not in service. | #greet#, #address#. The lamps are trimmed, so I'm my own for an hour.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's my own. Come, sit, and I'll find you a bite. | Ah, it's you. Come in by the fire, #pet#.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. I've done three rooms since. | Twice today. You're a #good# sight, both times.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. I'd hoped you'd pass this way. | #greet#. Bless you for stopping.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=servant] : #greet#. Quietly, now; the family's in. | #greet#. A word, and then back to #floors#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#, and mind how you go.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Sleep sound, neighbour. | #farewell#. Mind the dark corners.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. Nobody below stairs said a word. | #marvel#. That'll be round the servants' hall by supper.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. That's not reached our back door yet. | #oath#. Fancy that now.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. It was round the breakfast table below stairs. | It came up #backstair# with the breakfast trays.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait till somebody upstairs says so. | Field-talk, that's all, till somebody proves it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'm sorry for them. | #sympathy#. I'll keep them in mind tonight.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That's a ripe bit of cheer. | #good.capitalize#. Somebody deserves it, bless them.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. #floors.capitalize# shine and nobody's rung for me. | Well enough, #address#. Patient, as ever.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Guests in, and every room wanting doing. | Run off my paws. #bellpull.capitalize# hasn't stopped since dawn.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Keeping well? | How's the day been to you, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Here, take a sit and a breath. | That's a sour crop. I'm sorry, I truly am.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Every blight passes. | It'll come #good#. Give it a season.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I can't. The family's in, and I'm wanted in #chambers#. | I'd like to, truly. Only I'm on duty till the lamps.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. It'll keep. | No harm. Another day, then, bless you.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. That's kind past what I'd ask. | Bless you for that, #address#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. It cost me nothing. | It was nothing. I've two paws and an afternoon.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #floors.capitalize# won't polish themselves. | I'd better go; #bellpull# will be ringing.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | Early start tomorrow. I'll be off.
line @1 accept_preclose : Off you go, then. #farewell#. | Go on. I'll see you soon.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | #bc_true#
scene floors_done
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Did the long gallery this morning. #polish#, a cloth, and three hours on my knees. | The family walks on #floors# and never looks down. That's how I know they're done right. | I can tell who's crossed a floor by the paw-marks. I don't say so.
b : Three hours? | That's a strange sort of praise. | Wise not to.
a : Three, and worth every minute when the light comes in. | It's the only kind I get, and I'll take it. #saying.capitalize#. | Wise, bless me, and it keeps me in work.

scene the_bell
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #bellpull.capitalize# went eleven times before noon. Eleven, #address#. | They ring, I go, and half the time it's for a window open a pip too wide. | I've learned to hear #bellpull# in my sleep. I wake up halfway to the door.
b : That's a lot of stairs. | A pip too wide? | In your sleep?
a : A lot of stairs and a #good# pair of legs. I'll not complain. | Just so. I opened it a pip less. The family thanked me. | In my sleep. Then I stand there in the dark feeling daft as a scarecrow.

scene lucky_lump
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : See this? #hanky.capitalize#. There's #coal# inside, for luck. | I keep #coal# knotted up in my pocket. I'd feel bare without it. | I touch #coal# before I go into a room. Silly, maybe. It's never failed me.
b : Coal? For luck? | Why coal? | Never once?
a : Coal, bless you. A warm thing that's waiting to be warmer. That's luck to me. | My #gran# gave me a lump when I left home. Said I'd never be #cold# with it. | Not once that I know of. Mind, I'm careful, so it's hard to tell which of us is working.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha#

scene houses_winter
when topic=times|gossip here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / insist / ack
a : You'll see: before the winter's done, the Houses will have fallen out. | You can feel it #below#. Stewards whispering, letters going out at night. | I've a bad feeling about the Houses this year, and I'm not one for feelings.
b : They always squabble. | Letters at night? | Maybe you're wrong.
a : Squabble, yes. This is different, #address#. Nobody laughs about it now. | At night, sealed twice. I only carry the tray; I don't read. | I'd like to be. I'll keep #coal# close till I know.
b? : #bc_we_will_see# | #bc_hope_so# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene below_stairs
when topic=friends|work self.friend self.job=servant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# and I share the work and the jokes below stairs. A #good# arrangement. | I'd trust #self.friend# with my lump of coal. That's the most I can say of anyone. | #self.friend# keeps me steady when the house is in a temper.
b : Good to have someone. | That's high trust, from you. | Houses have tempers?
a : It is. Service is lonely without a friend on #backstair#. | It is. Don't tell anyone, mind. | This one does. You learn the weather of a house like the weather of a field.

scene the_neighbour_house
when topic=gossip|home self.neighbour here.region=ridgemere self.job=servant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I see #self.neighbour# on the stair some mornings. A nod, and on we go. | #self.neighbour#'s rooms are on my round. I do those rooms as careful as my own. | Not one word against #self.neighbour# from me. Not where walls could hear it, anyway.
b : A nod's enough. | Careful's right. | Nor would I.
a : Plenty, in a house like this. Everyone knows their place. | Always. The floors don't know whose they are. | Wise, neighbour. Walls listen in the big houses.

scene whittle_evening
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've #whittle# going of an evening. A wren, this one. Nearly done. | I whittle little birds and leave them on the sills for the maids to find. | I carved a spoon for the kitchen. It gets used for stirring and for pointing at me.
b : A wren? | Do they know it's you? | Pointing at you?
a : A wren. Small things are the hardest; you can't hide a slip. | They guess. I don't say. It's nicer as a mystery. | At me, when I'm late. It's a #good# spoon for it.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

scene fish_friday
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / invite / accept_invite / assess
a : #fish.capitalize#. If I could eat one thing for the rest of my days, that's it. | There's #fish# for the servants' supper once a week. I count the days. | I'll buy you #fish# off the stall on Restday. Nobody should eat it alone.
b : Every day? | Once a week's not much. | I'll take that.
a : Every day, and bread to mop the butter. | It's enough to look forward to. Come and have some, if the kitchen allows. | Ripe and right. Restday, then, by the stall.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_i_will# | #bc_good#

scene feast_bells
when topic=festival|season self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #bells.capitalize# get me up before the house, and I don't mind it one bit. | When #bells# go, I open the attic window and just listen. | There's nothing like #bells# carrying over the roofs. Back home they sounded the same.
b : They are lovely. | Just listen? | The same?
a : They are. They make the work feel like the feast's half mine. | Just listen. #polish.capitalize# can wait five minutes. | Near enough. A bell's a bell, bless it, wherever you are.

scene crowds_market
when topic=smalltalk|day self.dislikes=crowds here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I went to the market for the kitchen and got stuck in #crush# for a quarter hour. | I can't abide #crush#. Too many elbows, and none of them sorry. | When the streets are full I take the back lanes instead, however long it takes.
b : Markets are like that. | Nobody's ever sorry. | Long way round?
a : They are. I kept #coal# in my paw the whole time. | Not one. I said sorry for all of them. | Long, quiet, and nobody treads on me. Worth it.

scene waiting_on
when topic=work|day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : I spent an hour waiting on the family to decide which room they wanted. I could have done two. | Waiting on folk is harder work than any floor. | I'll do anything but stand and wait. #oath#, it's the worst of service.
b : An hour? | Harder? | I'd hate it too.
a : An hour. I counted the tiles. There's two hundred and six. | Harder. A floor gets done. Waiting never does. | You'd learn it. I have, mostly. Mostly.

scene summer_dusk
when topic=season|weather here.season=summer here.time=dusk self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #evening.capitalize#, and my duties done. That's the best hour in a whole season. | I sit on the back step once the lamps are done and watch the swifts. | Warm evenings like this I'd happily never go in.
b : The best? | Swifts? | Nor would I.
a : The best. Nobody rings, and the air smells of somewhere else. | Swifts, round and round the roofs. Back home they flew over the barley. | Then we'll sit out together till somebody calls us in.

scene rain_floors
when topic=weather here.outdoors=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / reassure / assess
a : #rain.capitalize#, and every boot in the house brings it in on #floors#. | Wet days I put mats at every door and still find paw-prints upstairs. | The rain here never stops long enough for #floors# to dry.
b : Can't you stop them? | Upstairs? | It's the city.
a : Not the family. You don't stop the family. I mop after. | Upstairs. Somebody's sneaking about, and it's not me. | It is. I'll keep #polish# handy and my patience handier.

scene home_south
when topic=memories|land self.away=yes self.from=southmeadow
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : In #self.from_town# the evenings were all swallows and stubble. I miss that more than I'd say. | I left #self.from_town# to go into service. My #mum# cried at the cart, and so did I. | Back home I'd never seen a carpet. Now I've three to beat before breakfast.
b[from=southmeadow] #home : Swallows and stubble. Bless you, I miss that too. | We all cried at that cart. | Nor me, till I came here.
b : Do you go back? | That's hard. | Three carpets?
a@home : Then we're a pair for missing it, neighbour. | Every one of us. And then we got on with it. | Ah, you know. We were all simple folk, bless us.
a : When I can. Not often enough. | It was. She writes now, which is #good#. | Three, and a rug the family likes beaten twice.

scene dream_cottage
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dream of a cottage with a bench by the door. Somewhere I don't hear a bell. | Some fine harvest I'll have a garden and nobody to wait on but myself. | I'd like a little place with an apple tree. I'd sit under it and whittle.
b : Where? | When? | Just whittle?
a : South, maybe. Somewhere the evenings are long. | When I've saved enough. Patience, bless me. I'm #good# at it. | Whittle and watch the apples. That's plenty.

scene faith_plain
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I say my prayers at night and keep #coal# in my pocket. The Bright One won't mind both. | The chapel's #good#, but I pray best on my knees with a cloth in my paw. | #good.capitalize# work and #bed# kept warm: both get thanked for at night. That's most of my praying.
b : I'm sure it won't. | Floor prayers. | That's enough.
a : I hope not. They've never quarrelled yet. | Floor prayers, aye. A clean floor's seen from up there, bless it. | I think so. The rest I leave alone.

scene gossip_careful
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : They're saying #below# that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I only heard it. | The kitchen says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd not swear to it. | A word on #backstair#: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all I know.
b : Do you believe it? | Why not? | Is that so?
a : I believe it was said. That's all I'll go so far as. | Because a kitchen will say anything to pass the morning. | So they say. I keep my nose in #polish# and out of it.
b : #bc_fair# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha#

story the_first_coal [topic=memories|pastimes self.away=yes self.from=southmeadow]
  : When I left home for service, my #gran# pressed #coal# into my paw and closed my fingers round it.
  : She said a wolf with a coal in the pocket never goes #cold# and never goes without.
  : I've had it ever since. Wrapped it in a handkerchief so it doesn't black my coat.
  ask : Would you have kept it, a thing like that?
  b : I would. You don't throw away a thing like that.
  b[old] : I'd have kept it. My own gran gave me a thimble. I still have it.
  : That's the way. Small things carry the big ones.

story the_dropped_tray [topic=work|memories self.job=servant]
  : In my first days at the house, I dropped a tray of glasses on the upper landing.
  : Every one went bouncing down, and not one broke. An old footman came out and just stared.
  : I closed my paw round #coal# and picked them up one by one. Nobody's ever believed me.
  b : I believe you. That's luck.
  b[job=servant] : Not one? I'd have been out on my ear.
  : Luck, or the stair was too well polished to hurt them. I did the polishing.

story the_feast_window [topic=festival|memories self.likes=festival_bells self.away=yes self.from=southmeadow]
  : The feast morning back home, my #dad# would carry me up the church tower to hear #bells# close.
  : I was frightened and I wouldn't let go of the rail, and I loved every minute.
  ask : Did anybody ever take you up somewhere high like that?
  b : Once. I was too scared to look down.
  b[stage=young] : Not yet. I'd like that.
  : That's what I feel every feast morning since. A bit frightened and very glad.

rule @floors_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Mind #floors#, please; they're just done. | Paws on the mat, bless you, paws on the mat.

rule @coal_bark
when concept=bark working=yes
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #oath#. Still there. #coal.capitalize#, safe. | Pocket, hanky, coal. Right, then.

rule @bell_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's #bellpull# again. Coming, coming. | Up #backstair# once more, then.

rule @crowd_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=crowds here.region=ridgemere here.day=market
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Excuse me. Excuse me, please. Bless me, what a crush. | #crush.capitalize#. I'll go round by the lanes.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Can I help you with something? | #greet#, #address#. Mind the floor, and say on.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Bless you, back again. What's wanted? | #topic.player#. A #good# sight. What can I do?
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, #address#. I'm off duty, so say what you need.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Yes? Quietly, if you please. The family's in.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=servant] : I'm #self.trade_words#. #floors.capitalize#, fires, linen, and the bell, all day long. | I keep #chambers#. You'd not know I'd been, and that's the point.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I'm patient about it. There's no more to it than that, bless me. | Whatever's wanted, done quiet and done well.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. It reached the kitchen door this morning.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : Everyone #below# is on about #world.event_words# today.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing I've heard, #address#. The house is quiet, bless it.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The kitchen says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd not swear to it.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I keep my ears to #floors# and my mouth shut, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind how you go. | #farewell#, #address#. Bless you.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that knotted in your handkerchief? -> lump
node lump
say A lump of coal, for luck. My #gran# gave it me when I went into service. I touch it before I go into a room.
mood warm
free
choice Does it work? -> lump_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node lump_why
say I've never dropped a thing that broke, and I've never gone #cold#. You can call that luck or care. I call it both.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
